From 4edca30146d21484eaff1c4cb82ca950992d33eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 04:25:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(properties): pre-launch is now driven by the RERA
 number, plus three fixed card flags
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rule, as specified: a project with no RERA registration number is in its
pre-launch phase, and so is one whose launch date is still in the future.
The is_prelaunch checkbox remains as a manual override.

One guard sits on top, and it matters. A blank rera_number in WordPress
means one of two things: genuinely unregistered, or nobody typed the
number in. Four projects are blank today and three of them — ACE
Golfshire, ACE Platinum, ACE Aspire — are Delivered or Ready to Move.
None appears in UP RERA's registered list, which is expected: a
registration lapses once a project completes. Labelling an occupied tower
PRE-LAUNCH would be a false claim on a lead-generating page, so a
delivered project is never pre-launch whatever its RERA field says. That
leaves exactly one genuine pre-launch project today.

Cards now always carry exactly one of three flags: PRE-LAUNCH, UNDER
CONSTRUCTION, READY TO MOVE. Previously the badge could be absent
entirely when possession text matched no pattern, which read as an
oversight, and a fourth 'NEW LAUNCH' state overlapped Under Construction.

The status filter follows suit. 'New Launch' is removed — it matched any
possession text containing '202', so 'December 2028' and '2022' both hit
it, filing delivered projects under construction. Pre-launch is not a
chip because those projects are held out of the grid and shown in their
own band below.

The homepage gains that same Pre-Launch band beneath the featured
projects, capped at three, hidden entirely when nothing qualifies.
